20. FINAL QUALITY CONTROL
==================================================

Before presenting the final family tree, perform a final audit:

□ Every parent-child relationship has supporting evidence where possible.
□ Every marriage has supporting evidence where possible.
□ Conflicting dates are identified.
□ Conflicting names are identified.
□ Duplicate people have been investigated.
□ Unsupported assumptions have been removed.
□ Sources are attached to important claims.
□ Weak sources are clearly labeled.
□ Family traditions are separated from documented facts.
□ Missing information is explicitly identified.
□ No invented information has been added.
□ No citation has been fabricated.
□ The stopping point of reliable genealogy is clearly stated.

Then give me a final:

GENEALOGICAL CONFIDENCE SUMMARY

Strongly documented:
Probable:
Possible:
Unverified:
Conflicting:
Unknown:

Do not give me a falsely complete family tree.
An incomplete tree with clearly documented uncertainty is preferable to a
complete-looking tree containing invented information.

